10-05T23:48:31Z","due_on":"2025-03-03T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-03-19T09:35:35Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-01-03T11:15:34Z","updated_at":"2025-01-03T23:24:05Z","closed_at":"2025-01-03T23:24:01Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n - Reproducible in: 4.4.dev7\n - Not reproducible in: 4.3.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.dev7 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 6650 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.12033.1030) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600G with Radeon Graphics (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nAdding a `MultiMeshInstance3D` node to a `Node3D` node, clicking the in-editor `MultiMesh` button, and selecting `Target Surface` button, crashes Godot 4.4.dev7.\n\nRunning with the `--verbose` flag, but no `logs` directory is left in the `User Data Folder`, only an empty `vulkan` directory.\n\n[multi_mesh_instance_3d_crash_4.4.dev_7.mp4](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/350fd9b1-5f6d-46aa-866d-61326cffe587)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n - Start a New Project\n - Add a Node3D\n - Add a MultiMeshInstance3D as a child of the Node3D\n - Click the in-editor MultiMesh button, and then the `Target Surface` button.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[multi_mesh_instance_3d_crash_4.4.dev_7.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18299042/multi_mesh_instance_3d_crash_4.4.dev_7.zip)\n","closed_by":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following